# ── Test artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Playwright traces/reports are large binary blobs (individual trace.zip files
# reach 50 MB). They are regenerated by running the suite and must never be
# committed - they previously accounted for ~1.1 GB of the repository.
playwright-report/
test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

# ── Benchmark output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The result JSON/CSV under benchmark-results/ IS tracked: it is the evidence
# behind the published performance numbers and is small (~370 KB).
# The rendered decks are regenerable from it (`npm run benchmark:slides` /
# `benchmark:marketing`), so they are not.
benchmark-results/slides/
benchmark-results/marketing/
benchmark-results/*.duckdb
benchmark-results/*.duckdb.wal

# Playwright run artifacts — regenerated by `npx playwright test`.
# The test sources under passmark-tests/tests/ ARE tracked; their output is not.
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
